f thinking that  because men and women are different it  means that a woman's  woman women are kind of naturally having  some maternal instinct that women are  naturally more suited to being in the  home or  kind of you have a child and immediately  everything about your life  changes and you never have any ambition  to work  or think again you know i really do  think that men and women can be equals  and can do everything um this you know  can  act the same in the world but i don't  think that means erasing the differences  between men and women  and so what would be sort of an ideal or  values that you  are aiming for because i guess one thing  that feminism  does bring to people is sort of an end  goal or the feeling of a movement in  which you're progressing towards  something  do you have like an alternative ideals  or values that  drive you forward yeah and you know i  think there would probably be  um ideals and values that 20 years ago  a lot of people would have labelled as  feminist so  i would like to see a world where my  sons and my daughter  can all do whatever they want to do  you know that there being a boy or a  girl a man or a woman  doesn't hold them back in any way  whatsoever that they can  lead happy and fulfilled lives in  work in hobbies and interests in  family you know whatever it means for  them individually to be  fulfilled and happy i really hope that  they would have an  absolutely equal opportunity to do that  my concern is that i'm not convinced  that is the end goal of feminism today  i think feminism has changed i think if  that was the  end goal of feminism it would actually  say we've pretty much  got there you know we pretty much are  at that state now i think the problem  for feminism  is that it kind of needs to dig up new  issues  to justify itself so it finds ever  smaller and narrower points to  expose um inequality so just yesterday  to give an example  uh there's a story in the newspaper  about air conditioning in offices 