e this message that they are just  because of how they were born um just  because of the society they live in  almost through no fault of their own  they carry this toxicity this kind of  poison to other people  i think some really a really harsh  message  to send to young to young men on the one  hand  it makes it very difficult for them to  negotiate growing up in a positive way  if they're told they're toxic before  they've even  entered the world and done anything but  i think it's also  really hard for young women because like  say it kind of imbues  young women with this sense that they  are victims in the world  um that they need to feel sorry for  themselves  that again as i've said already you know  that the world's a kind of conspiracy  against them  and so even before they start out in  life and  go and meet challenges in the world  they're told  that the world's difficult for them i  think that's really unhelpful  but yeah i'm a way of saying well that  makes me sound like i've got some kind  of personal animosity  with laura bates i don't have it's more  just the the project and she's not the  only one  who does this there are lots of people  who go around and kind of give this  message nowadays  lovely thank you for more debates  talks and interviews subscribe today to  the institute  of art and ideas at iai tv  you

